  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(-1.5<X\\le 0.5).$\n\n| $x$ | $-1.5$ | $-1$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ | $\\frac{13}{16}$ | $1$ |",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $X$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.5<X\\le 0.5) & =F(0.5)-F(-1.5) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
